{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Day of</b> — when they enthrone their king, so that they call that day 'the day of our king,' they make him drunk with wine; then he stretches out his hand with the mockers. And this word is of doubled [forms], for it is לוץ [to mock], whereas had it been מלוצצים it would be from forms whose ע is weak [i.e., ע״ו roots], derived from לץ [scoffer], whose root is ליץ; therefore it is of doubled למ\"ד. Therefore תופפות and מתופפות are two separate roots." "And the word <b>החלו</b> [made ill] — מחלי [they made ill]. Like <b>הראו</b> [they showed], and 'our king' is the object, and the princes are the agents." "<b>The princes made ill</b> — the king, from drunkenness. And like it: <b>מחלה לב</b> [a sick heart]; the form מחלה [makes ill] the heart, from the increased [i.e., Hifil] stem, which is החלה." "And the meaning of <b>חמת מיין</b> [heat of wine] — with the absence of bet in חמת, instead of חמת מלא יין. Its meaning is: like 'from the heat,' and it is in construct. Just as <b>דלת וסגור דלתך בעדך</b> [and shut your door behind you], and the witness joins <b>חמתך ואף שכר</b> [your heat and even beer], which is like this meaning."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "I read שימליכו as 'they enthrone'; the clause structure is compressed and the antecedent of וזאת המלה is ambiguous between לוצצים in the verse and forms Ibn Ezra cites.", 3 "The syntax of והעד מספח is uncertain; the reference appears to be to a verse such as Deut 29:18 pairing חמה with שכר, but the exact quotation and grammar of מספח here are obscure."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:33.951795107Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}